    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d868">

                <pb facs="0693" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.112 B61/51.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Ciudad
                                Juárez</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">El Paso,
                        Tex.</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-04-22"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 22, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Federal court of Mexico at Ciudad Juárez to-day released from custody
                    Lawrence Converse and Edward Blatt, arrested February 22 <pb facs="0694" n="612"
                        xml:id="pg612"/> and charged with sedition and who claimed to have been
                    taken from American soil. The same court also released Richard Brown, the nurse
                    arrested February 26, also charged with sedition.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas D.
                    Edwards.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
